{"slug":"ohdsi-hades","name":"OHDSI/Hades","what_it_is":"HADES (Health Analytics Data-to-Evidence Suite) is a collection of 35+ open-source R packages for large-scale observational research against OMOP CDM data, covering population characterization, causal effect estimation, and patient-level prediction.","components":["CohortMethod","SelfControlledCaseSeries","EvidenceSynthesis","PatientLevelPrediction","Characterization","CohortIncidence","Capr/CirceR","CohortGenerator","PheValuator","CohortDiagnostics","Achilles","DataQualityDashboard","EmpiricalCalibration","Cyclops","DatabaseConnector","SqlRender","Eunomia","FeatureExtraction","Strategus","OhdsiShinyAppBuilder"],"protocols":["OMOP CDM","OHDSI WebAPI/Atlas REST","JDBC/ODBC"],"measurement":["Incidence rates/proportions","Calibrated hazard/odds/risk ratios","AUROC/calibration for prediction","Sensitivity/specificity/PPV/NPV","Empirically calibrated p-values","DQ rule scores"],"modes":["Single-package standalone","Strategus multi-site orchestration","Interactive Shiny results review"],"constraints":["MySQL explicitly not supported","All data must be in OMOP CDM","R >= 4.4.1 supported target","Java required for DatabaseConnector/Cyclops","Some packages GitHub-only, not on CRAN"],"docker_services":[],"notable_absences":["No Docker","No REST API server","No Python SDK","No MySQL support"],"configuration":[],"fault_injection":[]}